&lt;h2 id="garden-description">Garden Description&lt;/h2>
&lt;p>According to local legend, the Argive maiden, Hyrnetho, died in an ancestral struggle and was buried on this site &lt;a href="http://data.perseus.org/citations/urn:cts:greekLit:tlg0525.tlg001.perseus-eng1:2.28">(Pausanias, 2.28.6-7)&lt;/a>. The sanctuary lay in the midst of a grove of wild olive trees. Established law, even in Roman times, forbade anyone to remove broken branches of these olives or any other trees in the grove.&lt;/p>
